 - Validate config at parse time (the boundary), not inside business logic
 - Parse raw data into domain types at the boundary
 - Do not re-export transport, storage, framework, or wire types through the public surface
+- When you integrate a system whose model differs from yours, translate its concepts into yours in one module at the boundary. Map its status codes, names, and states onto your existing domain types. Do not add its values to your domain types. Add a domain concept only when the other system exposes a difference your code must act on, and name it in your terms.
